If the robot charges slowly or abnormally, and the environmental temperature/battery operating temperature have a certain impact, you can try following the steps below:
1. Robot need to be used in environments above 0 ° C and below 40 ° C. When the weather is hot or cold, if placed in areas with direct sunlight such as balconies or sunrooms, the placement of the base station should be changed in a timely manner to avoid affecting charging;
2. If the robot is in the plumbing version and cannot change the base station location, it can be turned off and left in a cool area for two hours before being charged again (in hot summer weather, the room air conditioning can be turned on to cool down for a while);
3. If the robot experiences slow charging or a decrease in battery level after a period of use, please wipe the surface of the charging electrode to avoid oxidation;
4. Special attention: Turn off the valley charging mode to ensure that the robot can charge normally during non valley hours.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PS: To ensure smooth charging, please do not place it outdoors or in extremely hot, cold, or humid areas.

The abnormal water level of the cleaning tray is closely related to the sealing performance of the machine's sewage tank. It is recommended that you follow the following steps to ensure the sealing performance during sewage pumping:
1. Please remove the cleaning tray, check if the sewage outlet is blocked and clean it in a timely manner, and wipe the overflow sensor of the cleaning tray;
2. Open the upper cover of the sewage tank, check if the sealing ring on the upper cover of the sewage tank is loose or deformed, make sure to manually reset it in a timely manner, and wipe it clean with a cloth;
3. After pouring sewage, ensure that the sewage tank buckle is installed in place;
4. After placing the sewage tank in the base station, gently press down to ensure that the sewage tank is installed properly
5. It is necessary to ensure that the cleaning tray is installed properly, otherwise there may also be water leakage~
If the problem still persists, please inform our customer service again and help us to send you a replacement dirty water tank for you to try again~

There are five kinds of situations when the prohibited area is invalid:
1. Your map is not saved correctly or the exclusion zone is not set correctly, it is recommended to enter the APP to check whether the map exists, after the exclusion zone is set, whether there is a click "√" to save the exclusion zone you set.
2. your family area is relatively large, the network is not stable, not covering the whole family, set the no-zone / virtual wall when the host is not stable connection to the family wifi, resulting in the no-zone is not saved;
3. the machine is in the positioning state, positioning state will enter the prohibited area, after successful positioning, will not enter it.
4. check your map, whether the map is skewed, if there is a stacked map, you can restore the map, restore the map to normal square, the subsequent version of our software will be optimized it;
5. If you have saved more than one map, when the machine enters the corresponding map, the APP needs to switch to the corresponding map, otherwise it will lead to the invalidation of the prohibited area.

It is caused by abnormal cleaner bottle detection, please follow the following steps to troubleshoot:
1. Make sure the cleaner bottle is installed correctly and press the cleaner bottle to the place.
2. If there is no voice broadcast 'Dtergent bottle installed', and the Auto-Add Detergent in App cannot enabled, Judgment is the micro switch failure, need to replace the Water Hookup Kit;
3. If the voice broadcast 'Detergent bottle installed', but the Auto-Add Detergent in APP cannot enabled, Press the cleaner bottle again by hand to keep immobile,then the fault disappears, Judgment is the micro switch failure, need to replace the water hookup kit;

1.Open the upper cover of the robot, press the buckle to remove the dust bin;
2.Open the bin cover marked with the arrow and remove the debris inside;
3.Fill th dust bin with water, close the cover, shake the bin left and right, pour out, and repeat for several times;
Note: Wash the dust bin with water only. Do not add any detergent or clean the filter screen with a finger or brush.
4.Remove the filter screen as illustrated, spin off the water, dry the filter before installing it back to the bin for use.
Note: Ensure the filter is dried up (for at least 24 hours) before use.

